experiment: dwprobe

########## praise only (what a caregiver actually does) — central->vocal (NON-PARTICIPANT) ##########
  instrument        dwprobe   trial seed 00000000000a11ce   3 creatures per arm
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  session           120.0 s per arm x 3 creatures, one object throughout
  the question      does a session of ball-teaching write a DIFFERENT
                    weight change onto central->vocal than a session of
                    cube-teaching? If not, no training can separate them.

  seed  mean|dw|    corr(A,A')  corr(A,B)   verdict
  0     3.929e-02   0.397       0.366       same either way
  1     2.880e-02   0.315       0.272       same either way
  2     3.284e-02   0.370       0.339       same either way

  mean |dw| per synapse        3.364e-02
  corr(same object, redrawn)   0.361   <- the reproducibility ceiling
  corr(cube vs ball)           0.326

    Read the second against the first, never against 1.0. If they are
    equal, showing a cube and showing a ball write the same weight change
    and R-STDP cannot build a conditional mapping on this tract. If the
    object correlation is clearly lower, the rule does differentiate and
    G3's failure is downstream of it.

