  --- shapeprobe, 200000 ticks ---
experiment: shapeprobe
  instrument        shapeprobe   trial seed 0000000001357d57   100 frames per bank
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  no network and no ticks: signal processing on the same frames
  m3probe renders, to decide whether a new visual sense is worth
  building before one is built.

  every bank encoded into the same 256-neuron population, then pooled
  by a random sparse binary projection onto 126 units.

  bank               chans  population  d=0.15      d=0.40      shuffled    coherence   delta PR
  WORD (control)     24     1.000       1.000       1.000       0.420       0.207       181.8
  retina (shipped)   176    0.920       0.680       0.560       0.540       0.157       34.7
  retina, 12 coarse  12     0.820       0.740       0.580       0.540       0.057       29.7
  radial profile     12     0.920       0.980       0.940       0.420       0.050       42.7
  angular spectrum   8      0.960       0.760       0.740       0.460       0.361       79.4
  radial+angular     20     0.980       0.860       0.760       0.460       0.151       55.9

  best candidate: radial profile at 0.940 pooled, retina 0.560, word 1.000.
  the channel-count control (retina at 12 coarse channels) pools at
  0.580. The candidate has to beat THAT, not just the 176-channel
  retina, or the finding is 'use fewer channels'.

  shapeprobe SAYS BUILD — a coherent visual front-end is worth building.
  This gates a build; it is not a result about the creature. It
  compares feature banks rather than what a brain makes of them, and
  it lets the candidates segment the frame, which the retina cannot.
  Both favour the candidates, so a REFUSE is decisive and a BUILD is
  a licence to measure.
  [shapeprobe took 0.0 s]

