  --- errprobe, 600000 ticks ---
experiment: errprobe
  instrument        errprobe   trial seed 000000000135c0b9   100 trials per arm
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  architecture      vision->vocal on the TUFT; the interneuron pools
                    vision, which is the input it has to predict
  reference         burstprobe reads the RAW plateau at 0.913 across
                    three seeds. v40 is not trying to beat that with a
                    bigger signal, but with a cleaner one

    arm              trials  resid early resid late  ffi w in  ffi w out plat%    obj|resid   shuffled 
    soma             100     0.14308     0.12619     1.0000    1.0000    40.6     0.940       0.508    
    tuft, fixed      100     79.40311    69.12254    1.0000    1.0000    0.0      0.700       0.504    
    tuft, learning   100     0.16146     0.14256     0.0019    0.0019    27.9     0.980       0.492    

  resid is the mean |apical| at the larynx. `ffi w` is the mean pooling
  weight, and it is the control on the residual: a residual that fell
  while the weight did not move is the creature going quiet, not the
  circuit learning. obj|resid classifies cube against ball from the
  per-neuron residual, against a 32-permutation null.

  residual vs fixed arm  +99.8%   (learning must cancel what a fixed
                         weight on the same compartment does not)
  weight, birth -> end   0.0019 -> 0.0019
  plateau, learn/fixed   27.9% / 0.0%   (a compartment driven to a rail
                         by an uncalibrated prediction never fires)
  obj|resid, learn/soma  0.980 / 0.940   (the payoff, not a check)
  raw plateau reference  0.913 from burstprobe, three seeds

  PASS — the circuit runs and settles. Read that narrowly: the fixed
  arm is a broken configuration, not a rival, so beating it by 99.8%
  only says a learned weight is usable on a tuft where a fixed one is
  not (27.9% plateau against 0.0%).

  WHAT IT BUYS, against the arm that is a rival: obj|resid reads 0.980
  learning against 0.940 with the interneuron left at the soma. The
  converged weight is 0.0019 — the circuit finds almost nothing to
  cancel, and the residual is the raw apical signal with a rounding
  error taken off it.

  The scales are the reason to suspect rather than the mechanism. `ffi`
  is a pooled rate in Hz, order 1, while the apical input is a sparse
  tract's per-tick arrival, order 0.1 — so one scalar per neuron
  multiplying a smooth rate cannot track a bursty sparse input, and the
  cancelling weight it converges on is small because that is the best
  such a predictor can do. A predictor that could is one that sees the
  same spikes: an interneuron POPULATION sampled per target, which is
  what Sacramento's circuit actually has and what DnaModule::ffi_source
  is not. That is a body-plan change, not a genome field.
  [errprobe took 15.0 s]

