    lost at 25% blocked: 57%   at 50% blocked: 53%

  NEITHER NAMED MECHANISM SURVIVES, AND THAT STOPS THE BUILD.
  Silencing the blocked neurons recovers nothing (-0.8 SE), so the cost is
  not their PERTURBATION. And blocking twice as many costs no more
  (+1.0 SE; 57% of the lesson lost at a quarter blocked, 53% at a
  half), so it is not DILUTION either -- dilution is a quantitative claim
  and it predicts a curve this data does not have.

  So `mask-unaffordable`'s 59% is reproduced here at 57% and BOTH of the
  reasons it gave for its own number are now refused. The cost is
  ALL-OR-NOTHING in the blocked fraction: partitioning the group at all
  costs most of the lesson, and partitioning it further costs nothing more.

  DO NOT BUILD THE COMPARTMENT DECODER. It was motivated as a fix for a
  mechanism that turns out not to be the mechanism, and a readout that
  removes the non-participants would only help if their presence were the
  cost. The question worth the next run is why the cost is FLAT -- what
  breaks the moment the group stops being taught as one.
