  cost -- the creature's COMPUTE, in synapse-visits. The stated goal is a
  small creature on LOW POWER; footprint measures bytes and says this
  project has no memory budget, and nothing has ever measured operations.
  three terms   NEURON UPDATES, dense in neurons every tick (net:2259);
                DELIVERY, EVENT-DRIVEN, a spike across its fan-out
                (net:2532); PLASTICITY, dense in synapses per REWARD
                CASH-IN and NOT per tick (apply_reward_impl).
  the headline  the TOTAL and which term dominates. Every number is a count
                from one run, so no energy constant or hardware model.
  not claimed   synapse-visits are not JOULES. Some neuromorphic designs
                update per-synapse state in parallel and would not pay the
                dense term as a CPU does. Operations and sparsity only.

  STATIC    1102 neurons, 33248 synapses, mean fan-out 30.2
  REGIME    120000 ticks = 120.0 s simulated at dt 1.00 ms; asleep for 0.0%
  ACTIVITY  5.05 Hz mean firing, 0.0050 of neurons spiking per tick
  REWARD    258 cash-ins = 2.15/s at the established 150-tick cadence

  OPERATIONS per SIMULATED SECOND, by what each term scales with:
    NEURON UPDATES     1.102e+06   dense in NEURONS, every tick       82.2%
    DELIVERY           1.675e+05   EVENT-DRIVEN, spikes x fan-out     12.5%
    PLASTICITY         7.148e+04   dense in SYNAPSES, per cash-in      5.3%
    TOTAL              1.341e+06   operations per simulated second

  THE HEADLINE: 1.34e+06 operations per simulated second, dominated by NEURON INTEGRATION.

  AND THE SHAPE OF IT MATTERS MORE THAN THE SIZE. `step()` contains NO
  dense-in-synapses loop -- every loop in it was listed to check -- so the
  synaptic cost is EVENT-DRIVEN and the dense-in-synapses sweep is paid only
  when reward arrives, 2.15 times a second here. What is dense every tick is
  the NEURON integration, and that is bounded by 1102 neurons rather than by
  33248 synapses -- a factor of 30. For the stated low-power goal that is
  the favourable arrangement, and it is the one the creature has.

  WALL CLOCK on this machine: 2.9 s for 120.0 s simulated (41.42x real
  time), 18.0 ns per counted operation.

