experiment: gapwrite
  instrument        gapwrite   trial seed 000000000135bdb9   2000 trials
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  question          `blockflip` says the creature silences whichever half is
                    on the wrong side of the target. So do two lessons on
                    OPPOSITE sides write to different halves? `retain` says no
                    -- its lessons already are opposite (0.093 and 0.800) and
                    it is the protocol that produces the 0.22 wipe.
  what decides it   lesson B starts from A's endpoint, not from rest. The
                    upper half is already at ~1.6 Hz, so B can suppress the
                    LOWER half further (writes separate) or RESTORE the UPPER
                    half (B undoes A). This reads which.
  my prediction     RESTORE -- little room left to suppress, much to restore.
                    Written before the run, and it is the outcome that kills
                    the separation route, which is why it is stated first.
  the control       `A-idle` teaches A then leaves the gap UNREWARDED, so
                    passive relaxation cannot be read as B's doing. Every
                    number below is AB minus A-idle.

  PRE-REGISTERED, written before the run
    measured    dB = (profile at end of gap) - (profile at end of teaching),
                summed over each half, per seed.
    RESTORE     AB's UPPER-half dB exceeds A-idle's by >= +2.0 Hz and >= 3 SE
                -> B undoes A directly. The separation route is REFUSED and
                the 0.22 wipe has a mechanism.
    SEPARATE    AB's LOWER-half dB is below A-idle's by <= -2.0 Hz and >= 3 SE,
                AND the upper-half test above does NOT fire -> B writes beside
                A. Then the wipe is not an overwrite of the WRITE, which puts
                it in tension with storage-vs-expression's pure-overwrite
                reading and that tension becomes the next question.
    BOTH/NEITHER-> reported, no verdict. B doing both is a real possibility
                and it is not the same as either finding.
    sanity      A-idle's own dB is passive relaxation. `retention` says a
                taught sound is KEPT with no conflict, so this should be
                SMALL. If it is large, existing data is contradicted and that
                is reported rather than absorbed.

