experiment: maskretain
  instrument        maskretain   trial seed 0000000001351cd4   2000 trials
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  question          the conflict is a PURE OVERWRITE, so the damage is in the
                    WRITE and separating it is the remaining route. Before
                    asking what a mask must KNOW, ask what it COSTS.
  why this changed  the previous ladder could not answer its own question: a
                    half-group mask left every masked arm at the learning
                    floor, err taught 1.0635 against `off`'s 0.8615. So the
                    mask, not the index, was the binding constraint.
  the arithmetic    dF1 is a rate-weighted centroid over the F1 group, so
                    confining a lesson to a fraction of the group caps the
                    reachable |dF1|: 0.75 leaves 62%, 0.50 leaves 50%, 0.25
                    leaves 38% of the range. The lesson fits or it does not.
  the gate          err TAUGHT vs the unmasked arm, paired on seed, read as a
                    SHARE of what the unmasked creature learned. A cost near
                    100% means the lesson is gone, not merely reduced.
  the refusal       if 0.75 of the group already costs more than half the
                    lesson, no width both leaves room for a second lesson and
                    lets the first one learn, and write separation is refused
                    on this readout for a structural reason.

