     flattening is not the per-neuron TARGETING of the homeostat.

  INTRINSIC PLASTICITY IS THE COMPRESSION. With IP held off during wake
  `bias -> rate` goes 0.34 -> 0.91. The homeostat cancels the bias inside
  its range -- no clamp is hit, the pinned share stays 0.000 -- and every
  other drive-dependent inhibition on this module is already off in the
  genome.

  NOT A FIX: v50 relaxed this and learning got WORSE (+16.6 -> -2.3).
  What it licenses is subtler -- IP regulates each neuron's OWN rate, so
  it cancels the TILT along with the common mode. A homeostat on the
  GROUP's mean rate would leave the tilt intact, and that is a mechanism
  nobody has built.

