  THERE IS A SHARED TIME COURSE — utterances agree about their own
  shape at +1.000 against a null of -0.080. The larynx already produces
  structure across time, so the missing piece is a way to SHAPE it,
  not a generator to create it.

  shared time course, the fraction of an utterance's movement that
  other utterances agree with:
    no chain           4.5%
    chain in central   20.0%
    chain in vocal     65.9%

  A SHAPE, BUT AN INAUDIBLE ONE — utterances now agree about their own
  time course (65.9% against 4.5%), which they did not before, so the
  chain IS reaching the larynx and imposing a reproducible trajectory.
  It spans 5 Hz. Teaching moves a formant by ~70 Hz. The generator
  works and the coupling is far too weak to hear, which is a question
  about the route into the vocal groups, not about the sequence.
